# archive.org sign-in (optional)
#
# Some archive.org sources — the PlayStation one right now — are only served
# to logged-in accounts. Anonymous downloads from them fail with HTTP 403.
# To use those sources, put YOUR OWN archive.org session cookies here and
# rename this file to:  archive_cookies.txt
#
# How to get them (do this on a PC, not on the handheld):
#   1. Log in to archive.org in your browser.
#   2. Open the browser's developer tools (F12) -> Application/Storage -> Cookies
#      -> https://archive.org
#   3. Copy the values of these two cookies:  logged-in-user  and  logged-in-sig
#   4. Put them below, either on one line or one per line.
#
# Example (these are not real values):
#
# logged-in-user=you%40example.com
# logged-in-sig=1234567890abcdef...
#
#
# NOTES, please read:
#  - Do NOT put your password here. It is not used and would not work.
#  - The SD card has no file permissions: anyone who takes the card can read
#    this file. Treat these cookies like a password — they grant access to
#    your archive.org account until they expire or you log out.
#  - Logging out of archive.org in your browser invalidates them, which is
#    also how you revoke them if the card is lost.
#  - Downloads made with these cookies are tied to your account, the same as
#    if you downloaded in the browser.
#  - Connections are verified against the bundled cacert.pem. If that file is
#    missing, sign-in stays off rather than sending your cookies over an
#    unverified connection.
